# .github-guard — declarations github-guard reads (see the github-guard skill:
# https://github.com/antimatter-studios/agent-skills/blob/main/.claude/skills/github-guard/README.md).
# git-config format: check with `git config -f .github-guard --list`, and
# double-quote any value containing # or ;.

# Required status checks for main. A declaration beats discovery exactly.
#
# Discovery requires checks BY JOB NAME, which is a guess at the PR gate and
# drifts silently: a renamed job, an added workflow, or any future check
# reporting under the github-actions app changes what is required without
# anyone deciding to. This repository is the one that found what that costs —
# #197's audit went looking for coverage that reports a pass without executing
# what it claims to, and in five sibling repositories the answer was a
# settings-page list that had quietly stopped matching the jobs. A list nobody
# reviews is not a decision; it is a residue. Writing it down here puts it in
# front of a reviewer every time it changes.
#
# The three names below are the whole PR gate and nothing else. `ci.yml` is
# the only workflow that runs on `pull_request` (`release.yml` is tag- and
# dispatch-driven, so its checks can never report on a PR and must never be
# required — a required check that never reports is a permanent block, not a
# gate). Verified against this repository: the check-suite of the latest
# pull_request run returns exactly these three under app slug
# `github-actions`, and main's HEAD returns the same three.
#
# What each one is for, since "why is this required" is the question a future
# edit needs answered:
#
#   Build & Test   — the app-hosted suite on macos-26, including the extension
#                    targets. Carries the executed-case floor of 160
#                    (ci.yml, `xcresulttool ... passedTests`), so it refuses a
#                    run that stopped early instead of reporting no failures.
#   Library tests  — DiskJockeyLibrary, host-free, seconds rather than
#                    minutes. Carries the floor of 215 (XCTest's "Executed N
#                    tests" plus swift-testing's "Test run with N tests").
#   Shell scripts  — scripts/ steers the pipeline, and had no gate at all
#                    until it got one. Refuses a script that exits 0 without
#                    printing its own "all checks passed", and refuses a glob
#                    that matched fewer files than the suite has.
#
# Names must match the check-run names GitHub reports. These are job `name:`
# values with no matrix, so they are literal — unlike the sibling repositories'
# "test / <os>" job-matrix spelling, which is the shape that catches people out.
[checks]
	required = Build & Test
	required = Library tests
	required = Shell scripts
